  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Fetch identity and repeated payloads",
      "finding": "Fixed Bazel9.3 FetchEvent delegates identity to fetchId(url, downloader); success is stored only in its Fetch payload. The exception requires an ID containing only fetch, a dictionary fetch payload and no mixed event payload. A repeated pure Fetch event is retained in original derived-event order and separately records first_event/event/id/first_payload/payload/equality. Different success values are retained, not collapsed. TestResult, TestSummary and all other duplicate IDs still fail. The observed three pairs have the same URL/downloader and are reproduced from preserved derived BEP.",
      "qualification": "This concerns sanitized metadata identities, not test-attempt acceptance or a claim that every possible Fetch succeeded."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Remote output materialization",
      "finding": "Only one independent original Bazel argument is added. Bazel9.3 declares remote_download_regex as output-affecting and independent of remote_download_outputs, compiles whole-string predicates, applies them to output execPath and waits for downloads. The regex selects final and retry test log/XML under bazel-out/<configuration>/testlogs, and matches all 998+16 original references. It does not select binaries, cache_status, arbitrary output ZIPs or outside testlogs paths. Original .bazelrc remote_download_minimal remains.",
      "qualification": "This changes evidence download I/O. Missing remote objects, upstream skip/in-memory/BazelOutputService exceptions and files never produced can still fail; actual next-run local XML materialization is unproven. Original 139 absent XML files remain absent."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Source identity and unchanged execution",
      "finding": "B21 new source is intended as one direct child of ebd31; fetch-depth4 covers new-head→ebd31→cc658→67, and every parent/tree comparison remains exact. B23 continues actual PR merge checkout with parents[67,event-head], complete projection to3982 and all14 working-source pins. Each candidate changes only its diagnostic workflow leaf, preserves all10582 main67 leaves, original120-minute runner/job configuration, wrapper, targets, default retry/parallelism and assertion source.",
      "qualification": "These are computed candidate trees and existing parent identities; new branch/commit/merge publication belongs to root and must be verified separately."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Failure propagation and privacy",
      "finding": "B21 original invocation remains non-continue-on-error and exits its saved original status; collector missing-data/privacy failures remain job failures. B23 retains original outcomes, source checks, both artifact outcomes, privacy flag and exact zero original/tee receipts in its final gate. Private raw BEP remains outside upload roots. New repeated-Fetch metadata is derived only from already-sanitized events and then passes the unchanged whole-upload privacy gate. Existing regular-file/path, credential, gzip/zstd decoding and safe-for-upload logic remains byte-identical.",
      "qualification": "The privacy scope remains bounded to the existing recognized forms and known credential scanning; this review does not claim universal classification of arbitrary unknown secrets."
    }
  ],
